    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for coredns",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for coredns fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in coredns:\n\n- Update to version 1.14.7:\n  * plugin/acl, plugin/cache, plugin/file, plugin/forward, plugin/kubernetes:\n    assorted correctness fixes (stale-cache races, AXFR zone contamination,\n    DoH health-check TLS config, failover counter reset, ACL bypass via\n    autopath).\n  * New: plugin/shed (UDP overload protection), plugin/tls (ACME DNS-01),\n    plugin/timeouts maxtcpqueries, DoQ connection-level concurrency limits.\n- CVE-2026-41178: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/baggage header parsing did not\n  reject excessively large raw values, allowing a denial of service via\n  oversized input; fixed by the otel bump to v1.44.0 pulled in with\n  this update (boo#1276712)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-packagehub-543",
        "title": "Patchnames"
